CORE
main.cpp

^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ primary, declared: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ primary, defined: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ partial specialization: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line \d+ invoked through a base: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.5\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
typecheck_type now expands the template packs among the call arguments of a
decltype operand (template_mapt::expand_call_argument_packs, only_nontype)
before checking it.  g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept this program, and it
fails only its WRONG assertion.
